# Patch files carry diff syntax: context lines start with a space, so "space before tab"
# and lone-space lines are part of the format, not whitespace errors. They stay LF in every
# checkout: they apply to LF sources (AO's files, `git show` blobs), and a CRLF copy from
# core.autocrlf failed with "patch does not apply" on Windows while CI passed.
*.patch -whitespace eol=lf

# Pinned third-party releases are verified by SHA-256; checkouts must keep their exact bytes.
desktop-electron/assets/keysmith/** -text
